# Recognition cues and word maps for the code-task handlers (issue #1177).
#
# `cues` records hold the trigger phrases for one handler intent (lowercase,
# English and Russian side by side; an optional `role` splits a record into
# named lists — e.g. the shell composer needs action verbs and file-context
# tokens as a conjunction, the format converter needs the two directions).
# Phrases are matched as substrings of the normalized prompt (which collapses
# punctuation to spaces and lowercases) and of the raw prompt lowercased.
#
# `map` records hold the word→value vocabulary the composers consult —
# numbers, regex separators and classes, SQL comparatives, shell extensions,
# size units, and the test-property slugs. Rust holds no cue literals.
#
# `test_cases` records hold the sample inputs the test generator renders for
# each recognized problem shape.
#
# Read by the handlers in `rust/src/solver_handlers/` through
# `crate::seed::seed_files()`.
cues
